{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-104947-r4613709","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:German Potato Salad","sourcePageId":104947,"sourceRevision":"4613709","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-01-26T02:33:03Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:German%20Potato%20Salad&oldid=4613709","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:54:25.045Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:German recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for potato salad","Category:Recipes using bacon","Category:Recipes using beef broth and stock","Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock","Category:Recipes using mayonnaise","Category:Recipes using potato","Category:Recipes using prepared mustard","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes using vinegar","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes using wine","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Side dish recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"b0988532d6cfadea43f9d36a825a0f335cb5826299aa7351aa0dc9edc04ae68f","sourceWikitext":"{{recipe summary\n| category = Salad recipes\n| servings = 5\n| time = \n| difficulty = 2\n| image = \n| energy = \n| note = \n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''German potato salad''' is a popular variation of potato salad that is generally served warm. It is typically more sour and contains pork or bacon.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n*1 ¾ [[Cookbook:Pound|lbs]] (790 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) red [[Cookbook:Potato|potatoes]]\n*4 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Vegetable Oil|vegetable oil]]\n*1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Mayonnaise|mayonnaise]]\n*5 tbsp [[Cookbook:Cider vinegar|apple cider vinegar]]\n*2 tbsp [[Cookbook:White Wine|Riesling wine]]\n*4 tbsp [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]] [[Cookbook:Stock|stock]]\n*4 tbsp [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]] stock \n*8 tbsp [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Onion|red onion]]\n*¼ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*¼ tsp [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n*1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Flour|wheat flour]]\n*1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*1 tbsp coarse prepared [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard]]\n*1 tbsp chopped [[Cookbook:Green onion|green onions]]\n*¼ lb (113 g) uncooked chopped [[Cookbook:Bacon|bacon]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n#Peel, thinly slice, and [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] the potatoes about 17 minutes or until done but still somewhat firm. Drain, set aside, and allow to cool.\n#Cook the bacon until crisp. Crumble or chop.\n#Reserve a small amount of bacon grease and mix with flour, breaking up all clumps of flour. Cook briefly, but try to avoid browning.\n#Add chopped bacon and remaining ingredients and mix.\n#Cook for 20 minutes or until smooth at low heat.\n#Pour sauce over potatoes and stir gently.\n#Serve warm, room temperature, or cooled.\n\n[[Category:German recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using potato]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bacon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vinegar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wine]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for potato salad]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes usin